//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// DESIGN RULES
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

// • UUID primary keys for OLTP tables
// • BIGINT surrogate keys only for analytics fact tables
// • Monetary values use decimal(18,2)
// • JSONB for extensibility
// • Immutable financial records
// • Soft-delete omitted unless business requires it
// • Audit trail stored separately
// • All timestamps use timestamptz
// • Tenant isolation via tenant_id
// • Business identifiers (booking_no, invoice_no, etc.) are unique
// • Availability is projection-based, not computed on every query
// • Ledger follows double-entry accounting
// • External integrations are idempotent
// • Event publishing via Outbox Pattern
// • Read models can be rebuilt from immutable events

//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// END OF DBML
